        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Burlington, Vermont; Church Street; downtown Burlington\n- Buildings: Montgomery Ward Building\n- Projects: Church Street Marketplace\n- Organizations: Carr, Lynch Associates\n\nFacts:\n- The Church Street Marketplace in Burlington, Vermont, was initially conceived in 1958.\n- The Church Street Marketplace in Burlington, Vermont, was built in 1980–81 to a design by Carr, Lynch Associates of Cambridge, Massachusetts.\n- The Church Street Marketplace is an uncovered outdoor pedestrian shopping and dining mall consisting of the four blocks of Church Street between Main and Pearl Streets in Burlington, Vermont.\n- The Burlington Montgomery Ward Building is a historic former department store building at 52–54 Church Street between Cherry and Bank Streets in the Church Street Marketplace of downtown Burlington, Vermont.",
